.TH BRIXCVMFS 1 "2026-08-05" "brix client" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brixcvmfs \- CVMFS client mount and Stratum-0 release-manager tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brixcvmfs
\fIREPOSITORY\fR \fIMOUNTDIR\fR [\fIfuse-opts\fR]
.br
.B brixcvmfs
\fB\-\-rw\fR \fIREPOSITORY\fR \fIMOUNTDIR\fR [\fIfuse-opts\fR]
.br
.B brixcvmfs
\fB\-\-check\fR \fIREPOSITORY\fR
.br
.B brixcvmfs
\fB\-\-prewarm\fR \fIREPOSITORY\fR
.br
.B brixcvmfs repo
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brixcvmfs
is the CVMFS personality of the
.BR brixMount (1)
umbrella (same binary, selected by program name \(em
\fBbrixMount cvmfs \fR... is equivalent).  It mounts CVMFS repositories
read-only or with a local writable overlay, verifies them without
mounting (\fB\-\-check\fR), warms a cache (\fB\-\-prewarm\fR), and \(em via the
.B repo
subcommand family \(em creates and publishes repositories as a Stratum-0
release manager.  Everything runs unprivileged: mounts use FUSE3, and
publishing writes only ordinary files under the repository directory.
.SH REPO SUBCOMMANDS
The release-manager surface.  \fIREPO_DIR\fR is the repository storage
directory (conventionally \fI<webroot>/cvmfs/<fqrn>\fR so it can be served
directly); \fIKEYS_DIR\fR defaults to \fIREPO_DIR\fR\fB/keys\fR.
.TP
.B repo mkfs \fIFQRN\fR \fIREPO_DIR\fR [\fIKEYS_DIR\fR]
Create a repository: mint the RSA master key pair, repository certificate
and key (reused if already present in \fIKEYS_DIR\fR), the 30-day signed
whitelist, an empty root catalog and the signed manifest at revision 1.
The parent of \fIREPO_DIR\fR must exist; refuses to run over an existing
published repository.
.TP
.B repo info \fIREPO_DIR\fR [\fIKEYS_DIR\fR]
Print revision, root catalog, certificate and whitelist state, verifying
the full trust chain with the same parsers the client and proxy use.
.TP
.B repo resign \fIREPO_DIR\fR [\fIKEYS_DIR\fR]
Re-mint the whitelist (30-day expiry) and re-sign the manifest.  Run from
cron well inside the expiry window.
.TP
.B repo transaction \fIREPO_DIR\fR
Open a publish transaction: takes the single-publisher lock and creates
the staging tree \fIREPO_DIR\fR\fB/.brixtxn/upper\fR.  Stage changes by
writing ordinary files there; delete a published path by creating a
whiteout marker \fB.brix.wh.\fR\fINAME\fR in the corresponding directory.
.TP
.B repo abort \fIREPO_DIR\fR
Discard the open transaction (removes \fB.brixtxn\fR and the lock).
.TP
.B repo publish \fIREPO_DIR\fR [\fIKEYS_DIR\fR] [\fB\-\-chunk\-size\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-dirtab\fR \fIF\fR]
Turn the staged tree into the next revision: content-addressed objects,
rewritten catalogs (only the touched subtree), reflog append, manifest
re-sign, then an atomic manifest swap \(em a crashed publish never leaves a
half-visible revision.  \fB\-\-chunk\-size\fR \fIN\fR splits files larger
than \fIN\fR bytes into chunks (floor 4096); \fB\-\-dirtab\fR \fIF\fR applies
a \fB.cvmfsdirtab\fR-style nested-catalog split policy file.
.TP
.B repo fsck \fIREPO_DIR\fR [\fB\-\-data\fR]
Verify repository integrity: every catalog reachable from
\fB.cvmfspublished\fR is fetched and CAS-verified, its self/subtree counters
are recomputed from the actual rows, and xattr BLOBs are bounds-checked.
\fB\-\-data\fR extends the sweep to the payload: the certificate and every
referenced content object and file chunk is checked for presence and CAS
identity \(em the on-disk rot check, linear in repository size, so plain
\fBfsck\fR stays cheap enough to run after every publish and \fB\-\-data\fR
belongs in a slower cron.  Never writes to the repository.
.TP
.B repo gc \fIREPO_DIR\fR [\fIKEYS_DIR\fR] (\fB\-\-keep\fR \fIN\fR | \fB\-\-keep\-since\fR \fIT\fR) [\fB\-\-grace\fR \fIS\fR]
Reflog-anchored garbage collection: keep the newest \fIN\fR revisions (or
those newer than epoch \fIT\fR), drop the rest from the reflog, then sweep
unreferenced objects.  \fB\-\-grace\fR \fIS\fR protects objects younger than
\fIS\fR seconds.  Tagged revisions are always kept.  Refuses to run against
an open transaction.
.TP
.B repo tag add \fIREPO_DIR\fR \fINAME\fR [\fIKEYS_DIR\fR] [\fB\-m\fR \fIMESSAGE\fR]
Name the current revision as a snapshot.
.TP
.B repo tag list \fIREPO_DIR\fR
List snapshots (name, revision, root hash, timestamp, message).
.TP
.B repo tag rollback \fIREPO_DIR\fR \fINAME\fR [\fIKEYS_DIR\fR]
Republish the tagged revision's root catalog as a \fInew\fR revision (the
revision counter never rewinds).
.SH MOUNT OPTIONS
The mount forms accept the same \fIfuse-opts\fR as
.BR brixMount (1)
type \fBcvmfs\fR / \fBcvmfs\-rw\fR; see that page for the option table and
the overlay maintenance commands (\fB\-\-overlay\-list\fR,
\fB\-\-overlay\-reset\fR).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BRIXCVMFS_SERVER
Pin a single server URL for the repository (e.g.
\fBhttp://s0.example.org:8080/cvmfs/sw.example.org\fR).  The URL includes
the fully-qualified repository name.
.TP
.B BRIXCVMFS_PUBKEY
Path to the repository master public key (a \fB.pub\fR file, or a
directory of rotated \fB*.pub\fR keys).
.TP
.B BRIXCVMFS_CACHE
Local cache directory for mounts.
.TP
.B BRIXCVMFS_ETC
Configuration cascade root (default \fI/etc/cvmfs\fR layout).
.TP
.B BRIXCVMFS_TMP
Scratch directory override.
.SH EXAMPLE
An unprivileged single-node Stratum-0, from nothing to a mounted client:
.PP
.nf
mkdir -p ~/stratum0/cvmfs
brixcvmfs repo mkfs sw.example.org ~/stratum0/cvmfs/sw.example.org
brixcvmfs repo transaction ~/stratum0/cvmfs/sw.example.org
cp -r mytools ~/stratum0/cvmfs/sw.example.org/.brixtxn/upper/
brixcvmfs repo publish ~/stratum0/cvmfs/sw.example.org
# serve ~/stratum0 with nginx (brix_cvmfs_stratum0_root), then:
export BRIXCVMFS_SERVER=http://localhost:8080/cvmfs/sw.example.org
export BRIXCVMFS_PUBKEY=~/stratum0/cvmfs/sw.example.org/keys/sw.example.org.pub
brixcvmfs sw.example.org ~/sw
.fi
.PP
The full deployment cookbook (serving configuration, private repos,
replication, maintenance cron) is in the distribution's
\fIdocs/05-operations/cvmfs-stratum0.md\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success.  2 on a usage error or when the underlying driver fails.
Subcommands return non-zero on any refused or failed operation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR brixMount (1),
.BR fusermount3 (1),
.BR brix\-env (7)
